{"1949370": {"success": true, "data": {"type": "game", "name": "8/8/88 Needle AL", "steam_appid": 1949370, "required_age": 0, "is_free": true, "detailed_description": "Old Godfrey returns from his morning walk to find the town eerily deserted. Where did the townsfolk vanish to? And what could have caused such a devastating outcome? Unravel the twisted mystery and uncover the heart-wrenching tragedy that befell this cursed town.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nImmerse yourself in the stunningly realistic 3D photography of 8/8/88 Needle AL, a game that seamlessly blends the visual-novel and point-and-click adventure genres to create a dark gaming experience unlike any other. With a bone-chilling storyline about a cult, corruption, and racism in the post Civil War south, this game is a must-play for horror fans who loved our previous title &quot;Wardwell House&quot;.", "about_the_game": "Old Godfrey returns from his morning walk to find the town eerily deserted. Where did the townsfolk vanish to? And what could have caused such a devastating outcome? Unravel the twisted mystery and uncover the heart-wrenching tragedy that befell this cursed town.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nImmerse yourself in the stunningly realistic 3D photography of 8/8/88 Needle AL, a game that seamlessly blends the visual-novel and point-and-click adventure genres to create a dark gaming experience unlike any other. With a bone-chilling storyline about a cult, corruption, and racism in the post Civil War south, this game is a must-play for horror fans who loved our previous title &quot;Wardwell House&quot;.", "short_description": "On the ominous date of 8/8/1888, the entire population of Needle, Alabama seemingly vanished, leaving behind only a haunting silence and an eerie sense of dread. A first-person psychological-horror drama.", "supported_languages": "English<strong>*</strong><br><strong>*</strong>languages with full audio support", "header_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/ap